index e4b6604..eaf28a7 100644
--- a/docs/user/docs/midi-controller-mapping.md
+++ b/docs/user/docs/midi-controller-mapping.md
@@ -38,6 +38,7 @@ AetherSDR supports class-compliant USB MIDI controllers for hands-on control of
 - Binding table: **Parameter**, **MIDI Source**, **Channel**, **Invert**, **Relative**, an edit (**✎**) button and a delete (**×**) button
 - Category filter: All, RX, TX, Phone/CW, EQ, Global, Mode, Band, Filter, Slice, Display, Frequency
 - **Learn** / **Manual…** to add a binding, **Clear All** to remove every binding
+- **Visual Mapper…** — map controls on a picture of your controller (see below)
 - **Profile** row: **Save**, **Load**, **Import...**, **Export...**
 
 ## Adding bindings
@@ -61,6 +62,22 @@ Endless encoders send small "turned up / turned down" deltas instead of an absol
 
 The **VFO Tune Knob** parameter is meant for an endless encoder bound as **Relative**; as an absolute control it treats 64 as center.
 
+## Using the visual mapper
+
+**Visual Mapper…** opens a picture of your controller with the function bound to every knob, fader, wheel and button written above it.
+
+1. Pick your controller in **Controller**. AetherSDR ships a layout for the Hercules DJControl MP3 e2 (also MP3 LE and Glow).
+2. Click a control in the picture, or press or turn it on the controller itself while **Select a control by touching it on the controller** is ticked.
+3. Pick a function from the list on the right. The list shows only what that control can drive: buttons get on/off and press actions, knobs and faders get levels, and endless wheels get **VFO Tune Knob**.
+
+The change is live and saved immediately, and it shows in the binding table. Each function can be on one control only; picking a function already in use moves it to the selected control. **Reverse direction** flips a knob, fader or wheel, and **Unassign** clears the control.
+
+On controllers with key banks (the MP3 e2's **Loops/Fx** button switches the number keys between 1–4 and 5–8), use the bank buttons at the top or click the bank switch in the picture.
+
+**Photo…** puts a photo of your own controller behind the drawing. Take it straight from above and crop it to the controller's edges. It is stored in the `layouts` folder next to your profiles and can be removed with **Remove photo**.
+
+To add another controller, put a layout file in the `layouts` folder (`~/.config/AetherSDR/midi/layouts/` on Linux, `%LOCALAPPDATA%\AetherSDR\midi\layouts\` on Windows, `~/Library/Preferences/AetherSDR/midi/layouts/` on macOS). The format is described in `src/core/MidiControllerLayout.h`; `resources/midi-layouts/hercules-djcontrol-mp3-e2.json` is a complete example.
+
 ## Using profiles
 
 Save your bindings as named profiles to switch between controllers or layouts.
